| Feature                            | Load Balancer                                                 | Application Gateway                                          |
| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **OSI Layer**                      | Layer 4 (Transport - TCP/UDP)                                 | Layer 7 (Application - HTTP/HTTPS/WebSocket)                 |
| **Traffic Type**                   | Any TCP/UDP traffic                                           | HTTP/HTTPS traffic only                                      |
| **Routing**                        | Based on IP address and port                                  | Based on URL path, hostname, headers, cookies, etc.          |
| **SSL/TLS Termination**            | Limited or not supported (depends on implementation)          | Yes, supports SSL offloading/termination                     |
| **Web Application Firewall (WAF)** | No                                                            | Yes (often available as an option)                           |
| **Session Affinity**               | Basic                                                         | Advanced (cookie-based)                                      |
| **Performance**                    | Very high, low latency                                        | Slightly more processing due to application-layer inspection |
| **Common Use Cases**               | Load balancing VMs, databases, gaming servers, APIs using TCP | Hosting websites, microservices, reverse proxy, API routing  |


WAF ke main components
WAF Policy
Ye WAF ka main configuration object hai.
Isme security rules, custom rules, managed rules etc. define hote hain.
Managed Rules
Predefined security rules.
Common web attacks detect karte hain, jaise:
SQL Injection
Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
Command Injection
Azure mein generally OWASP CRS based rules use hote hain.
Custom Rules
Apne business/security requirement ke according rules banate hain.

Example:

If Source IP = 1.2.3.4
→ Block
Detection / Prevention Mode
Detection: attack ko detect/log karega, but traffic ko block nahi karega.
Prevention: malicious traffic ko detect karke block karega.
Exclusions
Kisi specific request parameter, header, cookie, URI etc. ko WAF inspection se exclude kar sakte ho.
False positives reduce karne ke liye useful.
Logs & Monitoring
WAF requests aur blocked traffic ke logs generate karta hai.
Azure Monitor / Log Analytics ke through analysis kar sakte ho.
